# ── DATABASE CREDENTIALS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The live neondb_owner password was committed in six plain .js/.sh scratch
# scripts and pushed for ~5 months. `.env*` above never covered them, because
# nobody put the credential in a .env file — they pasted it into a connection
# string in ordinary source. Ignoring these filenames is the cheap half of the
# fix; the half that actually works is tests/security/secret-guard.test.ts,
# which reads file CONTENT on every CI run.
.db_url
**/.db_url
db_url.txt
**/db_url.txt
credentials.json
credential.json
secrets.json
*.pem
*.key
!**/*.key.template

# Manufacturer asset PDF download cache (not source)
scripts/.mfr-cache/

# Deterministic pagination diagnostics (measured HTML + failing-sheet screenshots)
test-output/
